# foldctl_2tier_64_h4_up8000.topo -- the TREATMENT of the -rs_local_fold causal test.
#
# Identical to foldctl_2tier_64_h4_matched.topo except that the shared leaf<->top links
# run at 8000 Gbps, twice the 4000 Gbps host links, so no internal link can be
# saturated by streams the hosts feed at 4000. Radix_Up 2 / Radix_Down 8 keeps the
# bisection while halving the number of (now double-rate) uplinks.
#
# Result: the unfolded time is unchanged (35,205 -> 35,197 ns at |G|=16, S=16 MiB, i.e.
# still host-bound), but -rs_local_fold flips from +0.498 to -0.998 block times -- the
# full one-block saving. Slack on the shared link is what decides whether the fold's
# saving can be cashed; nothing else about the group or the tree changed.
Nodes 64
Tiers 2
Podsize 64

Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 4000
Radix_Down 4
Radix_Up 2
Downlink_Latency_ns 50
Switch_Latency_ns 300
Oversubscribed 2

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 8000
Radix_Down 8
Downlink_Latency_ns 50
Switch_Latency_ns 300
